{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>et My sabbaths you shall keep, etc.</b> One needs to know why the verse returns and commands here concerning Shabbat. It appears that the intention is to juxtapose the commandment of Shabbat to the commandment preceding it, as it is written ״לֹא תַעֲשׂוּ לָכֶם אֱלִילִים״ etc. — to say: just as idolatry is weighed against the entire Torah, so too the commandment of Shabbat is weighed against the entire Torah, all of it." "Further, it may also intend to speak of the sabbatical years, which are called sabbaths, as it is written (Leviticus 25:2) ״שַׁבָּת לַה׳״ — warning about them to keep them." "And juxtaposed to this warning He said <b>and you shall revere My sanctuary</b>, along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Avot ch. 5): the Temple was not destroyed except because they did not keep the commandment of the sabbatical year. And thus the verse states (Leviticus 26:34) ״אָז תִּרְצֶה הָאָרֶץ אֶת שַׁבְּתוֹתֶיהָ״. And He Himself said <b>et My sabbaths you shall keep and My sanctuary you shall revere</b> — that you not cause it to be destroyed when you fail to fulfill the commandment of the sabbaths. And you should know that although HaShem casts His wrath upon His house and His inheritance, to desecrate it as atonement for sin, as they said, of blessed memory (Midrash Tehillim 79), on the verse ״מִזְמוֹר לְאָסָף״ — despite all this, HaShem will bring into judgment all who cause, through their sin, this evil thing, on the awesome Day of Judgment, when the Master of the hallowed house will stand and the one who drove it out will be called to account. And how much more so in light of what the prophet said (Hosea 11) ״לֹא אָבוֹא בְּעִיר״, which they, of blessed memory, expounded (Zohar vol. 1, 1a): the Holy One, blessed be He, swore, etc. — where will He cast the disgrace, and what answer will be in His mouth, and what recompense will He assess against him? And this is what the verse alludes to here in saying ״וּמִקְדָּשִׁי תִּירָאוּ״ — for its punishment is great. From this one may gauge the punishment for shemittah, to keep it." "<b>Conclusion of the portion of Behar Sinai</b>"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {2 "The verse cited from Hosea (לֹא אָבוֹא בְּעִיר) is from Hosea 11:9; the reference given as הושע י\"א is chapter 11, matching."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:01:35.490004039Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}